# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
build/
dist/
dist-server/
coverage/
*.log

# Environment
.env*
!.env.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/

# Local caches
.cache/
# wrangler's own working directory: dev bundles, the local cache as sqlite, and its
# observability store. 5.6 MB after a few `wrangler dev` runs, none of it ours.
worker/.wrangler/

# AI assistant and tooling state.
#
# These are NOT harmless dotfiles. `.antigravity/` holds a multi-megabyte transcript of
# the assistant session — every prompt and reply verbatim — and `.impeccable/` records
# absolute paths that include the machine's user name. Publishing this repository with
# any of them tracked would publish that too.
.antigravity/
.claude/
.agents/
.codex/
.impeccable/
skills-lock.json
# AI Studio leaves an empty self-ignoring stub here; assets/ holds nothing else.
assets/

# Tooling that installed itself under .github/. The real CI workflow stays tracked;
# the 150-odd agent, hook and skill files beside it are local assistant config.
.github/agents/
.github/hooks/
.github/skills/

# One package manager: pnpm. That is what .github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml runs with
# `--frozen-lockfile`, so pnpm-lock.yaml MUST stay tracked. The other lockfiles are
# leftovers from experiments and would only make it ambiguous which tree is real.
bun.lock
package-lock.json

# The seeded design canvas is a build artifact, like dist/. It is 2.4 MB and loads
# support.js and vendor/react*.js, which the canvas tooling supplies at publish time and
# which are not in this repository — so the committed copy cannot open. The artboards it
# was built from stay tracked; re-seed with the design skill when they change.
design/rediseno-urbanos-lugo.html

# Backups written by the editing helper while working.
*.snapshot

# Diagram tooling. The QA renders it writes beside each diagram -- .visual-check.html,
# .visual-check.json and the PNGs at two sizes in both themes -- are how the tool checks
# its own output, not documentation. A single diagram brings 1.2 MB of them.
#
# The decision on the diagrams themselves: the JSON source and the two PNGs the README
# embeds stay tracked, the 700 KB self-contained viewer beside each one does not. Archify
# renders that viewer deterministically from the JSON -- delivering twice gave identical
# bytes -- which is the opposite of data/, where the snapshots are committed precisely
# because nothing can reproduce them.
docs/diagrams/*.visual-check.*
docs/diagrams/*.html

# The worker bundle. esbuild rebuilds it from worker/index.ts in seconds; committing it
# would be committing build output, which this repository does not do anywhere else.
worker/dist/
